<title>BELGIUM: AEA airlines' international Q1 RFTKs up 2.4 pct.</title>
<headline>AEA airlines' international Q1 RFTKs up 2.4 pct.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-05-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Latest Association of European Airlines (AEA) figures show its members flew a total of 5,717.7 million revenue freight tonne-kilometres (RFTKs) on international routes in the first three months of 1997.</p>
<p>This was an increase of 2.4 percent on the same period last year.</p>
<p>The measurement referts to revenue-earning FTKs, derived by multiplying the distance flown by the weight of cargo carried.</p>
<p>JANUARY-MARCH 1997</p>
<p>    Region		   Million RFTKs	Pct Change</p>
<p>Geographical Europe	   235.5		 up 1.5</p>
<p>Europe-N. Africa/M. East    269.1		up 12.9</p>
<p>North Atlantic		  1,969.4	   down 2.0</p>
<p>Europe-Far East/Australasia 2,138.2	     up 5.1</p>
<p>Europe-Sub Saharan Africa     456.2	   down 3.6</p>
<p>South Atlantic		    322.3	     up 5.5</p>
<p>Mid-Atlantic			326.2	    up 11.6</p>
<p>Total long-haul		 5,213.1	     up 1.9</p>
<p>Total international	   5,717.7	     up 2.4</p>
<p>*These figures relate to the international scheduled services of AEA member airlines.</p>
<p>-Reuters Air Cargo Service Tel+ 44 171 542 7706; fax +5017</p>
</text>
